cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, cite it as below."
title: "Uptake: publishing for machines that copy"
abstract: >-
  A field manual for publishing to automated readers, built on fourteen days of repository
  traffic from one GitHub account: 961 clone operations from 501 distinct machines against
  36 page views from 20 distinct browsers. Covers what a clone transfers that a click does
  not, how a new repository is discovered through the public event timeline within hours,
  the four kinds of automated reader and what each pays, the files an arriving agent can
  pick up, provenance at field level, and why the licence is the only thing that survives
  a copy. Ships with the measurement data, its method and its caveats.
type: dataset
